  {
    "id": "g-ser-estar",
    "title": "ser or estar?",
    "summary": "choosing the right \"to be\"",
    "intro": [
      "Use ser for what something is: identity, origin, job, character, the time.",
      "Use estar for how or where it is now: feelings, where someone is, the weather, states that change.",
      "Quick test: if it describes the person or thing in general, use ser. If it could be different in an hour, use estar."
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "O Pedro é alto.", "en": "Pedro is tall. (always: ser)" },
      { "pt": "O Pedro está cansado.", "en": "Pedro is tired. (right now: estar)" },
      { "pt": "A sopa é boa.", "en": "The soup is good. (a good soup in general)" },
      { "pt": "A sopa está boa.", "en": "The soup tastes good. (this bowl, now)" }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "For where a fixed place is, Portuguese uses ser or ficar, not estar: Onde é a estação? / Onde fica a estação?"
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O Pedro ", "after": " alto.", "options": ["é", "está"], "answer": "é", "en": "Pedro is tall.", "why": "Height describes him in general: ser." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Eu ", "after": " cansado.", "options": ["sou", "estou"], "answer": "estou", "en": "I'm tired.", "why": "How you feel right now: estar." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "A Rita ", "after": " de Coimbra.", "options": ["é", "está"], "answer": "é", "en": "Rita is from Coimbra.", "why": "Where someone comes from: ser." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Nós ", "after": " em casa.", "options": ["somos", "estamos"], "answer": "estamos", "en": "We're at home.", "why": "Where someone is now: estar." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O meu pai ", "after": " médico.", "options": ["é", "está"], "answer": "é", "en": "My father is a doctor.", "why": "A job: ser." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O café ", "after": " frio.", "options": ["é", "está"], "answer": "está", "en": "The coffee is cold.", "why": "A state that changes: estar." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Hoje ", "after": " sol.", "options": ["é", "está"], "answer": "está", "en": "It's sunny today.", "why": "The weather: estar." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "", "after": " três horas.", "options": ["São", "Estão"], "answer": "São", "en": "It's three o'clock.", "why": "The time: ser." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Tu ", "after": " muito simpático.", "options": ["és", "estás"], "answer": "és", "en": "You're very nice.", "why": "Character, in general: ser." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Vocês ", "after": " contentes?", "options": ["são", "estão"], "answer": "estão", "en": "Are you (all) pleased?", "why": "A feeling right now: estar." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-ter",
    "title": "ter",
    "summary": "to have, and to be hungry, cold, twenty…",
    "intro": [
      "Ter means \"to have\". Portuguese also uses it where English uses \"to be\": for age, hunger, thirst, feeling cold or hot, and fear."
    ],
